# Illegal: each literal is wider than the slot it was pinned to. Without the
# check these truncate silently - 256 stores 0, 300 stores 44 - in IR that is
# perfectly valid, so nothing downstream could catch it.
#
# All four are reported: one bad literal should not hide the next.
12:20: integer literal 256 does not fit in uint8
13:20: integer literal 300 does not fit in uint8
14:19: integer literal 128 does not fit in int8
15:22: integer literal -1 does not fit in uint16
